From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 00:30:00 +0200
Subject: usb: musb: Defer request giveback from queue/set_halt kick paths

Commit 3fc137386c46 ("usb: musb: Fix hardware lockup on first Rx
endpoint request") stopped musb_ep_restart() from calling rxstate() on
the OUT path and made it FLUSHFIFO the RX endpoint instead, to avoid
running the gadget's ->complete() callback synchronously from
usb_ep_queue() (which the API forbids and which could re-enter the RX
IRQ path and wedge the endpoint).

That flush is too big a hammer. f_mass_storage routinely pipelines the
next 31-byte CBW into the RX FIFO before its thread re-queues the
bulk-OUT request, so the flush silently discards a valid CBW and wedges
the link (spurious RXCSR / zero-length CBW / host reset).

This behavior was observed on Allwinner A64 SoC (Pinephone) but I assume
this will be a wider problem, because nothing suggests the code paths
are Allwinner specific.

Fix the original problem without dropping data: drain via rxstate() as
expected, but never hand a request back on the caller's stack from the
kick paths. Add a flag to rxstate() that when set it parks the finished
request on musb->gb_list and schedules gb_tasklet, which runs the
completions from softirq context -- where the IRQ-driven completions
effectively run too. After each completion the tasklet re-selects the
endpoint and re-arms rxstate() on the (possibly re-queued) head, so a
packet the host already left in the FIFO while the request ring was
briefly empty still gets drained.

I tried a workqueue, but that massively affected performance of USB
transfers, so in the end I opted for running completions in a tasklet
instead.

The IRQ-driven RX path (musb_g_rx) keeps completing synchronously
(defer_gb=false). Only the queue()/set_halt() kick paths defer.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.h   |  11 +
 drivers/usb/musb/musb_gadget.c | 190 ++++++++--
 2 files changed, 174 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.h b/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/musb_core.h
